# secrets.env.example - every variable the scripts and local runs read, by tier.
# Copy to .env (gitignored) and fill in only what you need. Placeholders only: this file is
# committed, so it must never hold a real value. `.env*` is ignored except this example.
#
# Tier A - always required: none. A fresh clone builds, tests and runs in memory with
#   nothing set, against the simulated partner.
#
# Tier B - required in CI / deploys only (set as GitHub secrets; named here, never valued):
#   FLY_API_TOKEN      deploy workflows (added by a later slice); without it deploy steps
#                      write a summary and exit green. Source: `flyctl tokens create deploy`.
#
# Tier C - optional (each degrades one feature, nothing else):
#   Auth__Authority    OIDC authority the API validates tokens against (added by the identity
#                      slice). Unset in Development = anonymous allowed, with a warning.
#   K6_BASE_URL        target of the k6 load scripts (added by a later slice).

# FLY_API_TOKEN=
# Auth__Authority=
# K6_BASE_URL=http://localhost:5000
